# Institution denylist — TEMPLATE (safe to commit; contains no real terms).
#
# Copy this file to `.institution-denylist` (which is gitignored) and
# replace the placeholders below with your real confidential terms. The
# pre-commit guard (scripts/check_no_institution_terms.py) reads the local
# copy and blocks any commit whose staged file contents, PATH NAMES, or
# commit message contain one of these terms.
#
# Format, one rule per line:
#   - Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#   - 're:<pattern>'  is a case-insensitive regular expression.
#   - anything else   is a case-insensitive literal substring.
#
# IMPORTANT — do not use \b for terms that can appear inside a path name.
# '_' is a regex word character, so '\bSITE_A\b' will NOT match
# 'configs/site_a_projection.yaml'. Use separator-aware lookarounds:
#
#     (?<![A-Za-z0-9])TERM(?![A-Za-z0-9])
#
# These fire at '_', '-', '/', '.' and string edges, while still refusing
# to match inside a longer word (so 'parasite_abdomen' stays clean).
# \b remains fine for prose-only terms such as work-item numbers.
#
# Keep the REAL list local only. Do not commit `.institution-denylist`.

# --- Organization names / abbreviations ---
# YourHealthSystemName
# YHS

# --- Campus / site codes ---
# Separator-aware so they also fire inside snake_case file names.
# re:(?<![A-Za-z0-9])SITE[_ -]?A(?![A-Za-z0-9])
# re:(?<![A-Za-z0-9])SITE[_ -]?B(?![A-Za-z0-9])

# --- Benchmark vendors under confidentiality ---
# BenchmarkVendorName

# --- Internal identifiers (example patterns — tune to your trackers) ---
# Work-item numbers like "Work Item 123456" or "WI-123456":
# re:\bwork[- ]?item[- #]*\d{4,}\b
# re:\bWI-\d{4,}\b

# --- Named individuals (add as needed) ---
# Firstname Lastname
